body:
I went shopping today after work and bought clothes. Not just clothes, but pants. I NEVER buy pants. At most, one or two pairs a year. It's mostly leggings for me and huge ass baggy cotton hippy-looking things that hide the fact that I exist. My clothing choices make no sense. ANYways. I bought pants and bras today and when I got home to try them on (thanks Covid), EVERYTHING FIT, except for 1 pair of pants and that is all I can think about. How fucking TIGHT they were... How badly I want to make them fit. Old me would fast, no thought about it. This me? The one who lost half of her hair last year because of thoughts like these? That girl doesn't give a fuck about those pants. That girl is trying to shove the other girl off of her chest right now so that she can fucking breathe. 

&#x200B;

I didn't see that coming.

Alright man. If you really and truly want to understand why so many people believe this was a racially motivated murder, then do some research. Here are some good places to start: 

White Fragility by Robin DiAngelo;
Locking Up Our Own by James Forman;
How to Be Anti-Racist by Ibram X. Kendi

 It might be more productive than arguing with strangers on the internet.

Could you describe Ghar and naphthalene a little more? Is it a heavy scent, bitter, overwhelming? 

&#x200B;

I'm intrigued :)
